This product is a Zigbee2MQTT port of control4-zha-quirks (Copyright 2026 the
control4-zha-quirks contributors, Apache License 2.0), and includes software
and documents derived from it: the device protocol logic now in src/, and the
SR250 / SR260 / keypad LED blueprints in blueprints/, which
tools/port-zha-blueprints.mjs ports from that project's ZHA blueprints.

control4-zha-quirks in turn includes software derived from the Control4 quirks
package in pvanbaren/zha-device-handlers (branch "control4",
zhaquirks/control4/),
https://github.com/pvanbaren/zha-device-handlers/tree/control4/zhaquirks/control4
itself part of a fork of zigpy/zha-device-handlers
(https://github.com/zigpy/zha-device-handlers), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. The SR260 blueprints and the upstream protocol
documents (C4-Z2IO-ZP, the APD120 dimmer, the SF120 fan controller, the scene
controller, the SR260 remote, the switched outlet) originate there.

Protocol knowledge was also drawn from the following projects, credited in the
documents and source where used. No code was copied from them:
- wmariz/zha-device-handlers (branch "control4"): the DIM1-Z paddle LED colour
  writer (c4.dm.l<btn><o|f>), LED write throttling, the KP6-Z reboot, and the
  LOZ-5D1-W outlet dimmer.
- bharat/homeassistant-control4-zigbee (formerly
  homeassistant-control4-dimmers, MIT) and his zigbee-herdsman-converters fork:
  the dimmer ramp map in its RESEARCH.md, the link-health failure modes in its
  issues, and the C4-KD120, C4-FPD120 and C4-V-ROSW120 notes.
- royceybaby/ha-c4-keypads: the dual-load C4-SDAPD240 and local keypad models.
- lights0123's and pstuart's SmartThings drivers: the LOZ-5D1-W and C4-KP2-Z
  check-ins.
- The Genesis Technologies "Control4 Zigbee - the definitive guide": pairing and
  reset button sequences.

